{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/180238-a-world-of-darkness-humanity-or-god-of-war","id":180238,"title":"A World of Darkness: Humanity or God Of War?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-25T18:13:24-07:00","id":180238,"title":"A World of Darkness: Humanity or God Of War?","content":"I been thinking a lot about this lately.<br /> This is a topic i always clash with and in which i have a lot of insights. Whenever i play a werewolf the apocalypse game, my DMs usually run it like God of War, a lot of battles, a lot of blood but a total disconnection of human society or almost as if they were background noise, no care for the human connections characters had in their past before &quot;Waking up.&quot;<br /> <br /> Here on chile we use a term for some Dms of VtM, some Dms run it like a game of constant war and battles with no politic elements what so ever. so we say that they run &quot;Vampire the Massacre&quot; instead of The Masquerade. Turning a game of &quot;Interview with a vampire&quot; to &quot;Underworld.&quot; or straight &quot;Blade.&quot;<br /> <br /> I been Dming Demon the fallen for a while, and i noticed that (In my experience and for how i understand the books) demon might be one of the most humanistic games since the need for demons to be with humans and sorounded by them. In my games i allow my players to create the demon characters (lore, name, faith and supernatural backgrounds as well merits and flaws) but I offer them pre designed humans for them to possess. this ones with their own families, jobs and such. hence the demons keep struggling between their Humanity against the need to face The Earthbounds or other purpouses.<br /> <br /> The question or the topic at hand is, How do you run a campaing? How important is the human element within a character? How important on your games are the side characters of a main character?, How important is the wife/husband, childrens, job etc...? and how do you keep it in balance?.<br /> <br /> Do you keep them as a background noise or front and center?, do you Batman the character (all his loved ones get killed ASAP)?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T18:31:51-07:00","id":180246,"title":"","content":"I've run a mix over the years. Mostly because running the same thing all the time is boring. One of the things about the cWOD that drew me to it so many years ago was that I had so many styles of game I could squeeze out it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T22:59:36-07:00","id":180462,"title":"","content":"It depends a lot on the players, sometimes the games are almost more about your interactions between the mortals around you and sometimes they are more about the supernatural community. Similarly as how it is important to strike a balance between action and politics/social connections, there are players who prefer social games and those who prefer action games usually both exists within the same group so it is important to find that balance. Same is true for supernatural/normal world. Either way I tend to never completely leave one or the other as a background noise but rather bring out the consequences for ignoring one or the other but like said the amount to which this comes up depends on the players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T06:46:02-07:00","id":180751,"title":"","content":"All depends I've done and played both. The only W20 game I've run was about a group of high school going through the First Change. The whole thing was more of a personal horror, focusing on them grappling with all that on their own. While the most recent game I've run was a Technocrat game that was more of an X-Files kind of story with several action scenes thrown in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T07:36:27-07:00","id":180798,"title":"","content":"It does indeed depend on the players, but generally I got for more drama than action. This can include human interaction, supernatural politicking, mysteries, romantic subplots and more. I have plenty of other games for action - and they often end up having a fair amount of drama too.<br /> <br /> I've run one straight-ahead action game of <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> and even that involved one character betraying another over a personal matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T05:55:09-07:00","id":181846,"title":"","content":"Frankly, I use them both.<br /> Most of my chronicles are &quot;social&quot; or &quot;detective-like&quot; punctuated, somewhere, by combat-situations<br /> then, there are some section where the combat situations (or preparation to a combat-situation) fill most of the time, while the social and investigation times are restricted.<br /> My players like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T08:48:16-07:00","id":182013,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">I\u2019ve said it before and I\u2019ll say it again:<br /> <br /> Splatterpunk.<br /> Gore.<br /> Fiesta.<br /> ARRIBA!!<br /> <br /> While my troupe\u2019s Sabbat games were unabashedly over-the-top and viscerally gonzo, our Wraiths were a bit more grounded. <br /> <br /> Most of the \u201chuman\u201d interaction came from us (the characters) dealing with ourselves. On the rare occasion when we did interact with the Skinlands, we tried to keep the theme of loss (from the character\u2019s perspective). Think <i>It\u2019s a Wonderful Life</i>, but gone wrong. Those moments were of the stereotypical \u2018bleak and depressing\u2019 variety. However nihilistically clich\u00e9d that might sound, at the end of these sessions we always felt better about our lives. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T01:49:16-07:00","id":187776,"title":"","content":"I try to emphasize the consequences of fighting in our world of camera phones and forensics. That drags my players kicking and screaming back down to earth if they need it, (like when one of my Archons blew up an NFL stadium to kill one Anarch), but it also teaches them how to do their fighting smart. If they decide go splatter-happy, I let them. Then I bring the heat down like it should realistically come down. If they kill the cops instead of bribing or tricking their way out of it, then next time it's the FBI. After that, Project Twilight steps in and things get real. Sometimes it makes for a very action-packed, fast-paced thriller. Sometimes it teaches a lesson and makes them better monsters. I leave it to them. When I ST, I try to be completely detached, impartial. I run the world as though the players hardly even exist and let them make their own game. I've had people dislike that method, wanting me to spoon-feed them a plot, but for the most part I've gotten really good feedback for just being the arbiter of causality. ... I like the sound of that. &quot;Arbiter of Causality.&quot; That's good t-shirt material... Er, anyway, keeping things human only works for me as far as the players let it. If they take the time to reflect, excellent. If not, nothing to do but find a different group to run that kind of story for.<br /> <br /> I tried to shoehorn a long-time friend of mine into playing more serious, thought-provoking games for years, but all he wanted to do was fight, blow things up, and joke around. In-Character joking around, mind you, not disruptive OOC chatter. His character was sardonic, very dark, and good at being very disarming with his ghoulish sense of humor. Once, his Toreador speed-metal guitarist went to Elysium because everyone else was going. Upon getting there, he put on a gargoyle-horned helmet he'd acquired from a previous scene and jumped onto the banquet table. There, he crouched like a gargoyle and began to feast on the master blood-prep chef's fineries like an animal. When approached by the Sheriff, he calmly looked up at the woman, slowly picked up a hotdog that had been put out for the Ghouls, pointedly skewered it onto one of the gargoyle helmet's horns, and stared intensely into her eyes. She wanted to be angry, but died laughing. (Another player.) It got him out of trouble, and he still got to be a complete jerk in Elysuim. (If only because the Prince was away and the Seneschal was Ravnos.) He himself is actually very kind and thoughtful, but when he games he wants to leave all that behind, cut loose, and vent his frustrations at the conformist world of Real Life (TM) for a while. I had to learn to not only accept, but embrace my players' personal preferences, and then I was able to organize different groups for different kinds of games and everyone had a good time -- myself included. That was my success story, I hope it helps!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3407-cerushad","name":"Cerushad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3407_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}